I collapsed the four trailing member copies into a single fixed-size `memcpy`, letting the compiler emit one wide load/store instead of multiple scalar loads/stores; the base-class copy is unchanged.

```include
#include <cstring>
```

```cpp
Field::Field(const Field &field)
    : FieldBase(field)
{
    std::memcpy(static_cast<void*>(&profile),
                static_cast<const void*>(&field.profile),
                sizeof(Field) - sizeof(FieldBase));
}
```